From: Dana Fried <dfried@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 07:00:12 -0700
Subject: [Views] Guard live menu updates against malicious AX callbacks

Use the new ViewGuard class to prevent AX code from synchronously
closing a menu that is being actively updated.

The previous ViewTracker was insufficient as there were calls whose
contents were not themselves protected; this approach is more
heavy-handed but will avoid any deletion of the menu under the call.

Bug: 577401536
Change-Id: Icc324f572c575f66cf37e1d9830db37049fa218d
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8670519
Reviewed-by: Amy Hwang <amyhwang@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Dana Fried <dfried@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1729086}

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
ViewGuard comes from the picked prerequisite d9fcba36b9c9
(https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8652648).

